  "body": "When I try to join `#homeowners:matrix.org` from my personal synapse, I got the following error:\n\n```\n2016-06-27 17:10:41,380 - synapse.http.outbound - 209 - INFO - POST-179- {GET-O-11} [dusky.horse] Result: 404 Not Found\n2016-06-27 17:10:41,382 - synapse.federation.federation_base - 87 - WARNING - POST-179- Failed to find copy of $1449625182125pvSkv:dusky.horse with valid signature\n2016-06-27 17:10:41,487 - synapse.http.server - 135 - ERROR - POST-179- Failed handle request synapse.http.server._async_render on <synapse.rest.ClientRestResource object at 0x7f8161dbb150>: <SynapseRequest at 0x7f8161db83b0 method=POST uri=/_matrix/client/r0/join/%23homeowners%3Amatrix.org?access_token=<redacted> clientproto=HTTP/1.0 site=8008>\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/hinmanm/.synapse/local/lib/python2.7/site-packages/synapse/http/server.py\", line 114, in wrapped_request_handler\n    yield request_handler(self, request)\nKeyError: '$1449625182125pvSkv:dusky.horse'\n```\n\nWhich caused the client (vector) not to be able to join the room. It's strange though, because a subsequent join succeeded.\n",
